Write a C program for a paint shop. The program should ask for the size of the area to be painted in square meters.
Consider that paint coverage is 1 liter for every 3 square meters and that paint is sold in 18-liter cans, which cost $80.00.
Inform the user of the quantity of paint cans to be purchased and the total price.

#include <stdio.h>
#include <math.h>

int main() {
    float area;
    float litros;
    int latas;
    float preco_total;
    
    printf("Enter the size of the area to be painted (in m2): ");
    scanf("%f", &area);
    
    litros = area / 3.0;
    latas = (int)ceil(litros / 18.0);
    preco_total = latas * 80.0;
    
    printf("Quantity of paint cans to buy: %d can(s)", latas);
    printf("\nTotal price: $ %.2f", preco_total);
    
    return 0;
}
